{"provider":"github","id":"5485","externalId":"5521889654","revision":"2026-10-12T22:20:19Z","type":"issue","title":"[Filed by Backprop] Windows supervisor reports false self-update skew on every box startup","body":"Filed by Backprop.\n\n## Problem\n\nOn every Windows box startup, the Scheduled Task supervisor emits:\n\n```text\nself-update skew: cannot read supervised daemon version at C:\\goobers\\goobers-support-approval-test\\updates\\current\\goobers.exe: C:\\goobers\\goobers-support-approval-test\\updates\\current\\goobers.exe: exit status 1: ; keeping existing binary\n```\n\nThe same binary is valid immediately afterward:\n\n```text\n$ goobers.exe version --json\n{\n  \"version\": \"v0.4.1-rc.3\",\n  \"commit\": \"02e0076a7421\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-09-18T21:24:56-07:00\",\n  \"goVersion\": \"go1.26.6\",\n  \"platform\": \"windows/amd64\"\n}\n# exit 0\n```\n\nThe supervisor then successfully starts that exact executable as the daemon. This reproduces on every machine reboot/startup, rather than being a one-off corrupt binary.\n\n## Root cause in current behavior\n\n`ensureCurrentBinary` performs one `version --json` subprocess probe with a 10-second context. Any failure is treated as unclassified skew and the existing binary is retained. There is no retry and the surfaced command error contains neither stdout nor stderr (`exit status 1: ;`), so a repeatable Windows startup/transient process-launch failure is indistinguishable from a bad supervised binary.\n\nThe fact that the same executable launches successfully immediately afterward establishes that this warning can be a false positive caused by the one-shot startup probe path.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Retry a failed supervised-binary version probe when the failure is transient and the binary still exists unchanged.\n- Preserve fail-closed behavior for malformed/missing version output and genuinely invalid binaries.\n- Include bounded, scrubbed stdout/stderr and the failure class in the warning.\n- Report whether failure was process launch, timeout, non-zero exit, or JSON validation.\n- Add a Windows regression where the first version probe exits 1 and the retry succeeds.\n- Avoid emitting `self-update skew` when no version skew was established.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Windows amd64\n- Scheduled Task supervisor\n- Supervisor action uses the installed Goobers binary with `__service-supervise`\n- Supervised slot: `updates\\current\\goobers.exe`\n- Supervised version: `v0.4.1-rc.3`, commit `02e0076a7421`","labels":["area:runner","goobers:approved","goobers:ready","goobers:claimed","type:bug","goobers:cloud"],"state":"open","status":"open","links":[{"rel":"self","url":"https://github.com/Agent-Clubhouse/Goobers/issues/5485"}],"url":"https://github.com/Agent-Clubhouse/Goobers/issues/5485","createdAt":"2026-09-21T01:56:14Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-12T22:20:19Z","readyAt":"2026-10-12T22:10:14Z","fields":{"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-09-21T01:56:14Z","id":5521889654,"issue_dependencies_summary.total_blocked_by":0,"locked":false,"number":5485,"state":"open","title":"[Filed by Backprop] Windows supervisor reports false self-update skew on every box startup","updated_at":"2026-10-12T22:20:19Z","user.login":"krishnapatel17"},"raw":{"id":5521889654,"number":5485,"title":"[Filed by Backprop] Windows supervisor reports false self-update skew on every box startup","body":"Filed by Backprop.\n\n## Problem\n\nOn every Windows box startup, the Scheduled Task supervisor emits:\n\n```text\nself-update skew: cannot read supervised daemon version at C:\\goobers\\goobers-support-approval-test\\updates\\current\\goobers.exe: C:\\goobers\\goobers-support-approval-test\\updates\\current\\goobers.exe: exit status 1: ; keeping existing binary\n```\n\nThe same binary is valid immediately afterward:\n\n```text\n$ goobers.exe version --json\n{\n  \"version\": \"v0.4.1-rc.3\",\n  \"commit\": \"02e0076a7421\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-09-18T21:24:56-07:00\",\n  \"goVersion\": \"go1.26.6\",\n  \"platform\": \"windows/amd64\"\n}\n# exit 0\n```\n\nThe supervisor then successfully starts that exact executable as the daemon. This reproduces on every machine reboot/startup, rather than being a one-off corrupt binary.\n\n## Root cause in current behavior\n\n`ensureCurrentBinary` performs one `version --json` subprocess probe with a 10-second context. Any failure is treated as unclassified skew and the existing binary is retained. There is no retry and the surfaced command error contains neither stdout nor stderr (`exit status 1: ;`), so a repeatable Windows startup/transient process-launch failure is indistinguishable from a bad supervised binary.\n\nThe fact that the same executable launches successfully immediately afterward establishes that this warning can be a false positive caused by the one-shot startup probe path.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Retry a failed supervised-binary version probe when the failure is transient and the binary still exists unchanged.\n- Preserve fail-closed behavior for malformed/missing version output and genuinely invalid binaries.\n- Include bounded, scrubbed stdout/stderr and the failure class in the warning.\n- Report whether failure was process launch, timeout, non-zero exit, or JSON validation.\n- Add a Windows regression where the first version probe exits 1 and the retry succeeds.\n- Avoid emitting `self-update skew` when no version skew was established.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Windows amd64\n- Scheduled Task supervisor\n- Supervisor action uses the installed Goobers binary with `__service-supervise`\n- Supervised slot: `updates\\current\\goobers.exe`\n- Supervised version: `v0.4.1-rc.3`, commit `02e0076a7421`","state":"open","state_reason":"","locked":false,"comments":5,"html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Clubhouse/Goobers/issues/5485","user":{"login":"krishnapatel17","type":"User"},"labels":[{"name":"area:runner","color":"1d76db","description":"Local runner: lifecycle, scheduler, stages, CLI"},{"name":"goobers:approved","color":"0E8A16","description":"Maintainer-approved — eligible for curation/implementation (SEC-047)"},{"name":"goobers:ready","color":"1D76DB","description":"Curated and scoped — eligible for implementation"},{"name":"goobers:claimed","color":"FBCA04","description":"Currently claimed by an in-flight run"},{"name":"type:bug","color":"D73A4A","description":"Defect in existing behavior"},{"name":"goobers:cloud","color":"1d76db","description":"Claim-partition: issue belongs to the cloud (Goobernetes) instance"}],"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T01:56:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T22:20:19Z","issue_dependencies_summary":{"total_blocked_by":0},"pull_request":null},"integrity":"maintainer"}